	(text "Test points (rear face, logic only): ±5 V, the expander's bus, STB1–3 and RST, buses A–H, GND"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.83 292.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "21ccad1d-a5d4-5ba2-8cf4-1f466717762f")
	)
	(text_box "CH446Q serial mode (P/S low): 7 address bits on CK, data on DAT, latched by STB; RST high = all open.\nTCA9534A 0x38: P0 DAT, P1 CK, P2 STB U7, P3 STB U8, P4 RST, P5 RUN, P6 BOOTSEL, P7 STB U12.\n  The mark (co-processor GPIO14) moved to the TCA9535 U6's P14.\nRUN and BOOTSEL are open drain emulated (output register 0, the pin switched to output).\n±5 V on purpose: at a single 5 V R_on is 120–225 Ω, and a 1.8 V board's I²C low would fail."
